OL,3,CProgramme listings for SUN 31 MAY
OL,4,G1500FMark Radcliffe's Nature Ramblings
OL,5,     GIn the first of three programmes
OL,6,     Gabout the natural world, Mark
OL,7,     GRadcliffe plays music inspired by
OL,8,     Gbirds. With works from Respighi,
OL,9,     GVivaldi , Elgar, Sam Lee and The
OL,10,     GUnthanks.
OL,11,G1600FJazz Record Requests
OL,12,     GAlyn Shipton presents jazz
OL,13,     Grecords of all styles as
OL,14,     Grequested by you. Get In Touch
OL,15,     Gvia jrr@bbc.co.uk or use
OL,16,     G_jazzrecordrequests on social.
OL,17,G1700FThe Early Music Show
OL,18,     GHannah French traces the life and
OL,19,     Gcareer of the Elizabethan
OL,20,     Gcomposer and organist Thomas
OL,21,     GWeelkes, who was born 450 years
OL,22,     Gago this year.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
